# smtputf8 -- offer the SMTPUTF8 extension (RFC 6531) in the EHLO response,
# so that clients may use UTF-8 in envelope addresses.  New in qpsmtpd 1.02.
#
# Leave this at 0 unless everything behind qpsmtpd can route non-ASCII
# addresses -- that means both the queue plugin in use and the MTA it feeds:
#
#   queue/smtp-forward   passes SMTPUTF8 on to the next hop and refuses to
#                        forward if that hop does not advertise it
#   queue/postfix-queue  needs postfix 3.0 or later
#   queue/qmail-queue    passes the octets through, but qmail cannot deliver
#                        them
#
# Non-ASCII envelope addresses are rejected while this is off; there is no
# downgrade to ASCII.  Message headers and bodies are unaffected either way,
# qpsmtpd treats message data as opaque octets and already offers 8BITMIME.
#
# See /usr/share/doc/qpsmtpd/config.md for the full description.
#
0
